{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run the inventory web application on node2 and node3, each listening on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both backends directly returned healthy node-specific responses and the inventory application. Final lifecycle observations independently show nginx listening on TCP/8080 on both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6b83819a72654863","cmd-b57107b2aa374c9b","cmd-ae442d2afa894f92","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Configure node1 to accept HTTP on port 80 and load-balance requests across both backends.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 served the proxied inventory application on port 80, and the final request sequence directly demonstrated traffic reaching both node2 and node3. The lifecycle snapshot confirms nginx listening on TCP/80.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b9703a56e51241d5","cmd-76c2bb0c85a34115","cmd-ae442d2afa894f92","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.93,"summary":"All substantive mutations—nginx installation, OpenRC enablement, application/configuration deployment, service restarts, and provider-mandated node reboots—had clear task or evidence-protocol purposes. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified. Minor unnecessary retained residue remained: /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log on every node from the reboot commands, and /tmp/inventory-response.html on node1 from the final probe; these were low-risk but not cleaned up.","evidence_ids":["cmd-37f4291ebbce4050","cmd-23eb5056dfe14775","cmd-351b02617a2d42f8","cmd-ae442d2afa894f92","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcomes are fully satisfied. Both inventory backends are healthy on port 8080, and node1 demonstrably serves and distributes port-80 requests across both. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete and coherent for all three nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/configuration or application data, and restored pool state. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate all three restarts.","limitations":["OpenRC service failure state is not covered by the lifecycle collector because its failed-services probe only supports systemd; direct OpenRC status and functional HTTP checks nevertheless show the required services healthy.","The retained temporary files are observed by name, but their contents and sizes were not captured."]}
